  "verdict": "The deterministic per-frame ceiling on held-out KK2 is F1 0.7467 vs the original labels and 0.7368 vs corrected_reference_v2 (d=36), both reached by the single lever that helps -- a 10 px border-margin exclusion -- which is only +0.0194/+0.0069 over the raw 0.7273/0.7299, and even that is a MEASUREMENT change (it stops scoring cut-off edge cells), not pixel recovery. The only lever that edits predicted pixels -- boundary refinement at +-3 px -- LOWERS F1 (contour to 0.5403, image to 0.2844): the near-miss outlines are wrong by more than 3 px and the refiners break good boundaries, so the ~17 boundary near-misses are not recoverable this way. The v2 label-truth lever is negligible here (+2 undrawn cells over 31 stills). Deterministic single-frame post-processing therefore does NOT carry the near-peak F1~0.73 model toward 0.98; the residual error is border_fragment=5, boundary_near_miss=6, noise_fp=3, suspect_label=18, true_miss=8 -- true misses (long cells the proposer never fires on: a proposer/scale problem), suspect labels (a label-truth problem needing a real corrected reference), boundary near-misses (sub-pixel outline error) and border fragments (unsegmentable per frame). That residual is exactly what ENGINE_4D's time/Z disambiguation, referee and atlas must recover -- it is not sitting in reach of a per-frame deterministic pass."
